   "daf": "22b",
   "sentenceId": 1,
   "he": "וְאָחִיו הוּא לְכׇל דָּבָר. לְמַאי הִלְכְתָא? לְיוֹרְשׁוֹ וְלִיטָּמֵא לוֹ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna stated that «he is his brother in all respects.» The Gemara asks: «With regard to what halakha» was this said? The Gemara answers: «To inherit» from «him, and to become ritually impure for him» if he is a priest, as a brother is one of the relations for whom a priest is permitted to become ritually impure by attending his funeral."
  }
